# cron.d entry for Lilith automatic escalation, for systems not using
# systemd. Install as its own file rather than appended to a shared crontab:
# /etc/cron.d/lilith-auto-escalate, or /usr/local/etc/cron.d/lilith-auto-escalate
# on FreeBSD. The fifth field is the user to run as.
#
# Runs every five minutes. The -m 60 window only bounds how far back each
# run scans; the per-alert auto_escalated marker is what prevents an alert
# from being escalated twice, so a generous window is safe and mostly
# matters for CAPE alerts whose 'stop' time can lag ingestion. Add
# `--config /path/to/lilith.toml` (before the subcommand) for a non default
# config file.

*/5 * * * * lilith /usr/local/bin/lilith auto_escalate -m 60
